#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110719 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110372 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ff4e9141-5743-55f1-a8be-3e28cb047eca" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Equations With Infinitely Many Solutions"}] :question/id #uuid "6355ac1e-bb4d-5133-9917-04dfb2bc5a0d" :question/math-academy-id "e-18854" :question/problem "Which of the following equations has infinitely many solutions?\n\n- $4x + 1 = 4x + 1$\n\n- $-3x = -4x + 6$\n\n- $2x + 7 = 2x - 1$" :question/worked-solution "Let's attempt to solve each equation in turn:\n\n- For the first equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x+1 & =4x+1 \\\\ 4x+1-4x & =4x+1-4x \\\\ 1 & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation is true for all values of $x.$ Therefore, the equation $4x + 1 = 4x + 1$ has infinitely many solutions.\n\n- For the second equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3x & =-4x+6 \\\\ -3x+4x & =-4x+6+4x \\\\ x & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation $-3x = -4x + 6$ has the unique solution $x = 6.$\n\n- For the third equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x+7 & =2x-1 \\\\ 2x+7-2x & =2x-1-2x \\\\ 7 & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation is false for all values of $x.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ff4e9141-5743-55f1-a8be-3e28cb047eca" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048213}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186111133 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ff4e9141-5743-55f1-a8be-3e28cb047eca" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Equations With Infinitely Many Solutions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5ec6698b-966d-5e31-b760-5faeba4367be" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438040} {:answer/id #uuid "ce68107b-c73c-5910-8bb8-b2dd40c29da8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438041}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5ec6698b-966d-5e31-b760-5faeba4367be" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438040} :answer-field/id #uuid "15760992-2dd2-5d43-b2a8-1b987c48791a" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439049} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c5f4a2b7-9944-5e1c-9ff0-88248a565319" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438042} {:answer/id #uuid "46c6e30e-5409-5621-86de-fccef2076faa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438043}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "46c6e30e-5409-5621-86de-fccef2076faa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438043} :answer-field/id #uuid "73a78852-4a44-54f0-a170-8df3bd3710e3" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439050} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "95fb5bb7-a16c-591d-9bc5-3cc80a4f1c75" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438044} {:answer/id #uuid "40143427-1f60-591b-865b-52bd73399fa8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438045}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "95fb5bb7-a16c-591d-9bc5-3cc80a4f1c75" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438044} :answer-field/id #uuid "f7b0dbf4-aa8c-5f41-bd3d-257a796c46ed" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439051}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "71c3d793-6b55-5392-ac94-1149b022497f" :question/math-academy-id "q-287966" :question/problem "Which of the following equations has infinitely many solutions?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $2x=x+1$\n- **II.** $2x+1=2x+1$\n- **III.** $2x+1=2x+3$" :question/worked-solution "Let's attempt to solve each equation in turn:\n\n- For the first equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x & =x+1 \\\\ 2x-x & =x+1-x \\\\ x & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation $2x=x+1$ has the unique solution $x=1.$\n\n- For the second equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x+1 & =2x+1 \\\\ 2x+1-2x & =2x+1-2x \\\\ 1 & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation is true for all values of $x.$ Therefore, the equation $2x+1=2x+1$ has infinitely many solutions.\n\n- For the third equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x+1 & =2x+3 \\\\ 2x+1-2x & =2x+3-2x \\\\ 1 & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation is false for all values of $x.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186111138 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ff4e9141-5743-55f1-a8be-3e28cb047eca" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Equations With Infinitely Many Solutions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "801c1341-5837-5b3c-bdca-f820a9ee8871" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438076} {:answer/id #uuid "48e9078a-e6f9-59fb-af05-9029d3a48e04" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438077}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "801c1341-5837-5b3c-bdca-f820a9ee8871" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438076} :answer-field/id #uuid "e865206f-261e-52b1-ae6e-68e8b33c31b3" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439067} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1d05df7f-dec5-59ce-b63b-c00fa9f8a672" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438078} {:answer/id #uuid "36e2ee78-8b01-5053-aa94-5d0e687cddc5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438079}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "36e2ee78-8b01-5053-aa94-5d0e687cddc5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438079} :answer-field/id #uuid "e502be4e-9bbd-5dbb-bb41-0769be49d17b" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439068} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a8ec9a73-6fbc-5213-bad0-073cc49fb549" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438080} {:answer/id #uuid "29a60663-a01a-5898-a8b1-97b46dadd573" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438081}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a8ec9a73-6fbc-5213-bad0-073cc49fb549" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438080} :answer-field/id #uuid "5bcded34-504d-5f90-a10a-87a266602706" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439069}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6b24019f-f592-514c-8874-109e97014d8f" :question/math-academy-id "q-288419" :question/problem "Which of the following equations has infinitely many solutions?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $3x=2x+5$\n- **II.** $4x-2=4x-2$\n- **III.** $5x+3=5x+1$" :question/worked-solution "Let's attempt to solve each equation in turn:\n\n- For the first equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x & =2x+5 \\\\ 3x-2x & =2x+5-2x \\\\ x & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation $3x=2x+5$ has the unique solution $x=5.$\n\n- For the second equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x-2 & =4x-2 \\\\ 4x-2-4x & =4x-2-4x \\\\ -2 & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation is true for all values of $x.$ Therefore, the equation $4x-2=4x-2$ has infinitely many solutions.\n\n- For the third equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5x+3 & =5x+1 \\\\ 5x+3-5x & =5x+1-5x \\\\ 3 & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation is false for all values of $x.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297181 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ff4e9141-5743-55f1-a8be-3e28cb047eca" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Equations With Infinitely Many Solutions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "51b73290-8884-52b0-bea9-586ed1106191" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438082} {:answer/id #uuid "84594a5c-0472-579f-8c56-3c27f2aa0b2f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438083}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "51b73290-8884-52b0-bea9-586ed1106191" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438082} :answer-field/id #uuid "d237ec26-3cf6-575e-bb01-acccb260545f" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439070} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6aa4deae-76c0-5bf7-a4af-1158715b25d4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438084} {:answer/id #uuid "e6ba602a-8c17-5e28-b8db-32b4e57396a8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438085}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6aa4deae-76c0-5bf7-a4af-1158715b25d4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438084} :answer-field/id #uuid "e0236bbe-ed0c-5681-b717-8d06a5afcad6" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439071} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "18b5cb76-d351-5058-a991-9afc4efc993e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438086} {:answer/id #uuid "b1790360-3d45-5107-959e-c1c762336309" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438087}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "18b5cb76-d351-5058-a991-9afc4efc993e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438086} :answer-field/id #uuid "ae99ebca-b507-5034-9f94-d990616ca1d6" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439072}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d5426119-4ea0-5c84-bb6c-cf460c622db0" :question/math-academy-id "q-288425" :question/problem "Which of the following equations has infinitely many solutions?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $-3x+2=-3x+7$\n- **II.** $6x+1=6x+5$\n- **III.** $7x-4=6x-6$" :question/worked-solution "Let's attempt to solve each equation in turn:\n\n- For the first equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3x+2 & =-3x+7 \\\\ -3x+2+3x & =-3x+7+3x \\\\ 2 & =7.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation is false for all values of $x.$\n\n- For the second equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6x+1 & =6x+5 \\\\ 6x+1-6x & =6x+5-6x \\\\ 1 & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation is false for all values of $x.$\n\n- For the third equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7x-4 & =6x-6 \\\\ 7x-4-6x & =6x-6-6x \\\\ x-4 & =-6 \\\\ x-4+4 & =-6+4 \\\\ x & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation $7x-4=6x-6$ has the unique solution $x=-2.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297182 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ff4e9141-5743-55f1-a8be-3e28cb047eca" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Equations With Infinitely Many Solutions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "86bc7e66-5bdd-5da7-b6ee-6b1a37c5ae9c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438088} {:answer/id #uuid "1dc3c549-6f72-5c75-9824-c4564938c74a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438089}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "86bc7e66-5bdd-5da7-b6ee-6b1a37c5ae9c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438088} :answer-field/id #uuid "01d95513-0985-54ed-85b5-aee1f0de0676" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439073} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "93091e42-4e1d-50af-874b-052e5b4ccf7b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438090} {:answer/id #uuid "831cc9b8-0274-570c-a213-da0beeeda4c0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438091}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "93091e42-4e1d-50af-874b-052e5b4ccf7b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438090} :answer-field/id #uuid "9ccfd62c-12fc-5d4f-a40e-e4d63caedad3" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439074} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1844e447-1273-5f4a-9121-461fc7343eef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438092} {:answer/id #uuid "fbfbb123-d421-50c5-bb94-58c01fc307f7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438093}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fbfbb123-d421-50c5-bb94-58c01fc307f7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438093} :answer-field/id #uuid "a73ad185-931c-5fc2-9419-95cfddabcee6" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439075}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "31ef6d07-7ebc-5067-b0a5-3f361bec8d1c" :question/math-academy-id "q-288427" :question/problem "Which of the following equations has infinitely many solutions?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $2x-5=x-2$\n- **II.** $6x+1=6x+9$\n- **III.** $-4x+3=-4x+3$" :question/worked-solution "Let's attempt to solve each equation in turn:\n\n- For the first equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x-5 & =x-2 \\\\ 2x-5-x & =x-2-x \\\\ x-5 & =-2 \\\\ x-5+5 & =-2+5 \\\\ x & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation $2x-5=x-2$ has the unique solution $x=3.$\n\n- For the second equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6x+1 & =6x+9 \\\\ 6x+1-6x & =6x+9-6x \\\\ 1 & =9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation is false for all values of $x.$\n\n- For the third equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-4x+3 & =-4x+3 \\\\ -4x+3+4x & =-4x+3+4x \\\\ 3 & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation is true for all values of $x.$ Therefore, the equation $-4x+3=-4x+3$ has infinitely many solutions.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297196 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ff4e9141-5743-55f1-a8be-3e28cb047eca" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Equations With Infinitely Many Solutions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f505619a-0f8f-5b06-bcd1-9ed29f3a46e2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438094} {:answer/id #uuid "800b7f50-dd11-50d4-910a-43bdf1c22e22" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438095}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f505619a-0f8f-5b06-bcd1-9ed29f3a46e2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438094} :answer-field/id #uuid "5d40aab5-2a51-5f28-9398-9e1f95aef724" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439076} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "35bdc9da-af4c-51a3-977a-aab317bf1688" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438096} {:answer/id #uuid "b473c870-043e-51e2-b1e7-8129f88a2f5f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438097}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "35bdc9da-af4c-51a3-977a-aab317bf1688" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438096} :answer-field/id #uuid "f63c5f3b-e9f0-5d44-b9b5-69d5b9503e16" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439077} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ca3aa2f5-1e64-5717-a73e-d38a34cd3c61" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438098} {:answer/id #uuid "14f6741b-26e8-5eea-b15d-fa64a12ad311" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438099}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "14f6741b-26e8-5eea-b15d-fa64a12ad311" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438099} :answer-field/id #uuid "6515f165-1d78-588e-8621-8c95e0aa4812" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439078}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "43eccfac-bd80-5f7b-abff-3250eee5dc70" :question/math-academy-id "q-288591" :question/problem "Which of the following equations has infinitely many solutions?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $3x+2=4x+1$\n- **II.** $2x-5=3x-3$\n- **III.** $5x-4=5x-4$" :question/worked-solution "Let's attempt to solve each equation in turn:\n\n- For the first equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x+2 & =4x+1 \\\\ 3x+2-3x & =4x+1-3x \\\\ 2 & =x+1 \\\\ 2-1 & =x+1-1 \\\\ x & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation $3x+2=4x+1$ has the unique solution $x=1.$\n\n- For the second equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x-5 & =3x-3 \\\\ 2x-5-2x & =3x-3-2x \\\\ -5 & =x-3 \\\\ -5+3 & =x-3+3 \\\\ x & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation $2x-5=3x-3$ has the unique solution $x=-2.$\n\n- For the third equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5x-4 & =5x-4 \\\\ 5x-4-5x & =5x-4-5x \\\\ -4 & =-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation is true for all values of $x.$ Therefore, the equation $5x-4=5x-4$ has infinitely many solutions.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""}] :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Equations With Infinitely Many Solutions"}]}
